# Zone 1, room 3 (grey box, Phase 1 task 7): tech 3, pogo chain. Rebuilt 2026-10-20 after the
# director's play ("The low roof is way too difficult and the lineup is almost impossible.").
# BUILD.md s5, tech 3: "Bounce off a line of enemies or hazards. Taught by a spike pit with Snuffed
# in it"; s15: "a 10-bounce chain across the zone 1 spike pit is possible at 4 bounces per second";
# s3: a hidden or optional place holds "a guaranteed Lantern-tier Votive or a Lamplighter note".
# Stand-ins: the spikes are the line of Snuffed (a hazard is pogo-able as an enemy is); no enemy
# stands in the pit yet; the reward is an entity marker (Phase 1 has no pickups), as in room 04.
#
# Two routes, one hall to start. West door at the foot of the hall (x 0), floor 672 u.
#
# THE MAIN ROUTE (the door to the east door): a short patch of 3 spikes (tiles 9 to 11; a hop over
# it, or one down-strike on it, is the safe first encounter: a hazard only sends Ash back to the
# hall's floor), then the hall's edge (x 576 u) and an OPEN pit 2496 u wide (78 tiles) with spikes
# along its floor and nothing above it for 320 u or more, where the longest bounce rises 131 u and
# a bounce with its air jump 257 u (the upper level's floor is the only roof, 288 u over the hall's
# floor). The entry lines itself up: the pit's first 8 tiles are 128 u deep, so a run off the edge
# falls about 17 frames to the spikes and the down-strike has a 10-frame window (pressed 4 to 13
# frames before the spikes touch; 03_main_route_early at 12 and 03_main_route_late at 4); the spike line then rises to 64 u
# below the floor, and its last 4 tiles to 32 u, so the last bounce has a lip to land past. A chain
# at the natural pace is 8 bounces, one every 36 frames (333 u at the run speed, 1.6 a second,
# about 5 seconds): zone1_03_main_route. Every bounce lands where the spikes are, whatever the phase
# of the run-up (checked from six start points and three press times); a missed bounce costs a
# heart and the run back from where Ash last stood (03_main_control_missed_bounce).
# Why 2496 u: with open air above, the width is the only thing that can stop a route without the
# pogo. tools/replay/gap_reach.gd on test/longpit (this pit with no far side) finds the strongest
# such route: a ground dash-jump, the air jump, the air dash and the Ember Toss reach 2432 u past
# the edge at the floor's height (03_main_control_no_pogo_toss falls at x 3018 u, 54 u short of the
# far wall); without the Toss 2243 u (03_main_control_no_pogo falls at x 2856 u); a carried jump
# 1333 u, a running jump 1201 u. A crossing needs more than the width less half the body (10 u), so
# 2496 u leaves the strongest route 54 u short; a shorter pit would be crossed by it. That fixes
# the length of the chain, not its pace: 8 bounces at the run speed, fewer at a dash-jump's.
#
# THE OPTIONAL PATH (the 10-bounce chain at 4 a second, s15): above the hall, a ladder of three
# one-way platforms in a 96 u well (tiles 5 to 7; tops 576, 480 and 384 u; the upper level's floor
# is 320 u) leads to the upper level: a hall, then the low tunnel (94 tiles, 3008 u, x 576 to 3584
# u) with spikes on its whole floor and its ceiling 64 u above them, then a low hall with the
# reward (a Lantern-tier Votive at x 4160 u) past a 3-tile shaft that is the way back: it drops 352
# u to the main east hall, beside the east door (03_optional_way_back). It is also a way in: a jump,
# the air jump and an up air dash lift the feet 404 u, so the whole kit climbs it (ADR-0016: the
# room teaches, it does not gate). The ladder stands 320 u
# and more west of the pit's edge, so no platform is a launch pad for the main pit. Missing the
# chain costs only a hazard (back to the upper hall's floor); nothing is behind it that the main
# route needs. The tunnel is the old room's, moved up 11 tiles (fixtures: spawn y 608 became 320):
# the player (44 u) can rise 20 u above the spikes and no more, so a jump, a dash-jump or the air
# jump cannot arc over them, and a bounce (794 u/s) rises to the ceiling and falls back in 13
# frames.
# Why the tunnel needs pogo: the farthest non-pogo route found (a ground dash-jump, its air jump, the
# air dash and the Ember Toss, searched over every tick that matters) ends 672 u into the tunnel,
# 2336 u short of its far end (tests/replay/zone1/03_control_no_pogo.fixture).
# Why the tunnel is 3008 u (the s15 line, ADR-0019 Decision 5): 20 u/f is the most speed Ash has
# (the dash-jump's, kept by every bounce), so a bounce every 15 frames, 4 a second, carries 300 u
# a bounce. The first bounce lands at x 771 u. Ten bounces at 4 a second reach x 3471 u and the
# tenth arc ends 187 u past the tunnel's end (3584 u): the chain crosses, bounce count 10, rate
# 4.0, 20 u/f kept on all ten (zone1_03_pogo_chain_route; an air jump 5 frames after each bounce
# holds each link to 15 frames, a down-strike on the fall ends it). Nine fall into the spikes at
# x 3451 u, 133 u short (zone1_03_control_nine_bounces).
# What else is possible: the plain chain (a down-strike and nothing else, a bounce every 13
# frames, 4.6 a second) covers 260 u a bounce and takes 11 (zone1_03_route_plain_chain; ten fall
# 233 u short, zone1_03_control_plain_ten). Faster is not shorter. Slower is: every air dash and
# air dash-jump spent between bounces makes the link 26 frames and 520 u, so 6 bounces at 2.3 a
# second cross (zone1_03_route_fewest_bounces; five fall short, zone1_03_control_five_slow), and
# nine bounces at 4 a second cross if the last arc is that slow (zone1_03_route_slow_finisher).
# The opening link is just as slow-able and needs no air dash: the no-pogo controls' dash-jump
# plus its air jump (dash 44, jump 49, air jump 61) land the first bounce on frame 72 at x 1027.5
# u, 256 u farther in than the route's 771.5, and nine bounces at 4 a second then cross, the
# ninth arc landing at x about 3745 u (zone1_03_route_slow_opener; eight fall in).
# The line counts bounces at 4 a second, so the optional path asks ten of a chain whose links are
# all 15 frames from a first bounce on the dash-jump's own arc (frame 57), not of every chain: a
# player who slows one link, the first or the last, buys 220 to 256 u with it. Geometry cannot
# forbid that without taking the air jump or the air dash away (a pit long enough to need ten after
# the slow opening, 3170 to 3195 u, leaves the route 25 u of slack).
room zone1/03_pogo_chain
size 132 28
spawn 96 672
tiles
